{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":256813,"duration_api_ms":376998,"num_turns":8,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"fd73935f-8aeb-44e3-b9bf-48ee748882a7","total_cost_usd":0.9455082499999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":5164,"cache_creation_input_tokens":38234,"cache_read_input_tokens":123933,"output_tokens":10265,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":38234,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":276,"outputTokens":16218,"cacheReadInputTokens":1278820,"cacheCreationInputTokens":122309,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.36213424999999994,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":5164,"outputTokens":10265,"cacheReadInputTokens":123933,"cacheCreationInputTokens":38234,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.583374,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Reviewed four amendments against the tank-simulation codebase. Two address real defects (CleanFilter mass loss and zero-effect action guard suppression) and should be accepted. Two are rejected: the test restructuring suggestion is a style preference with no functional impact given the linear math, and the dissolved_feed_residue_g_total amendment is based on an incorrect premise — siphoning doesn't remove dissolved organics in the model, and the tracker mathematically cannot exceed the actual DOC+DON pools it shadows.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-5-0fe11abb","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified in engine.rs: CleanFilter reduces all four microbe guild biomasses by intensity*0.5 but the removed mass is simply deleted — not routed to dissolved organics or detritus. The N and C content silently vanishes. The budget guard is bypassed because 'action:clean_filter' is listed as an open-system exception in tick_has_closed_system_nitrogen. The fix is straightforward: route setback biomass to DON/DOC pools using the existing route_live_biomass_to_dissolved_organics pattern (nitrogen_cycle.rs:482-495), and either remove the open-system exclusion or add an explicit export ledger entry. This is a genuine mass conservation defect."},{"amendment_id":"fr-5-367bd26c","decision":"reject","rationale":"The test aggregates all four microbe guilds into one sum then calls manual_live_biomass_nitrogen_mg once, while production code computes per-guild with max(0.0) clamping. However, the underlying formula organic_nitrogen_mg(mass * 0.20, ratio) = mass * 0.20 * 1000 * ratio / (1+ratio) is strictly linear. For non-negative inputs (which biomass values always are), sum-then-compute and compute-then-sum yield identical results. The max(0.0) clamp is a no-op for valid biomass. The test correctly validates total nitrogen accounting. Splitting per-guild is a style preference that adds test maintenance cost without catching any real defect. Negative biomass would indicate a bug elsewhere, not in the budget computation being tested."},{"amendment_id":"fr-5-047f391e","decision":"reject","rationale":"The amendment claims dissolved_feed_residue_g_total can exceed actual DOC+DON after siphoning, but this is mathematically impossible given the code structure. SiphonDetritus only removes particulate_organics and fine_detritus (solid matter) — it does NOT remove dissolved_organic_nitrogen or dissolved_organic_carbon from the water. Since siphoning leaves actual DOC/DON unchanged, the tracker correctly stays unchanged too. Furthermore, dissolved_feed_residue_g_total is decremented by the FULL mineralization consumption amount (nitrogen_cycle.rs:119-121) even though some consumed DOC/DON came from non-feed sources (plants, algae, microfauna, shrimp), so the tracker is always ≤ total DOC+DON. The suggested fix of decrementing the tracker during siphoning would make it LESS accurate by reducing it when the dissolved organics it tracks are not actually removed."},{"amendment_id":"fr-5-2e08bd46","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified in engine.rs: tick_has_closed_system_nitrogen (lines 523-535) checks entry.label strings to determine if a tick is open-system, but zero-effect actions like Feed{grams:0.0}, WaterChangePercent{percent:0.0}, SiphonDetritus{fraction:0.0}, etc. still record their labels via maybe_record_stage_with_explicit_budget. The label presence alone causes the guard to treat the tick as open-system, even though zero-delta actions leave the system materially closed. This means any no-op action silently disables conservation checking for that entire tick, potentially masking real N/C imbalances from other processes in the same tick. The fix to check BudgetEntry.delta magnitude (or original action parameters) instead of just label presence is correct and important for maintaining the integrity of the budget guard."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"ec42da43-488f-4ce2-b0ad-27febfdf3042"}
